      "construction": [
        "Reuse the original local SNL6 drum registration without refitting. Rear high-control pin pixel1490,908 is now a construction constraint, NOT a holdout. Dotted upper silhouette remains discrepant and may show another pose; it is not claimed validated.",
        "Revise only distal M355A/B profile and lower two joining-rivet stations. Upper pivots, brake adjustment, spring/saddle and first two rivets remain unchanged.",
        "Restore actual clutch floor attachment. Saved floor is527.05..533.05, while prior feet began584.4194307. Preserve main and auxiliary journal centers and all functional upper clutch connections.",
        "SH953A lower casting uses two floor pads and a raised bridge around the existing rear channel. Move its rear screw pair12.45mm aft, preserving four source-sized screws. Upper anchor lugs retained above the bridge. This is an unproven mounting/profile hypothesis.",
        "M4135 bored tab sits38.1mm aft of unchanged riveted foot on a raised return. This leaves room for a smooth rod bend before the clutch auxiliary lever. Both guides share one definition.",
        "Complete M575 travels from the real rear fork socket through the guide to the high intermediate rocker. Gentle end transitions and a dip under the clutch shaft are estimates constrained by retained solids. Static only; no motion or force validation.",
        "Nominal cylindrical thread envelopes; real thread helices and spring free rate/preload unknown."
      ],
